🧩 1. Understand DevOps Concepts

Before jumping into tools, understand what DevOps is and why it matters.

Learn:

What is DevOps, CI/CD, and Infrastructure as Code (IaC)

DevOps lifecycle: Plan → Code → Build → Test → Release → Deploy → Operate → Monitor

Agile & Scrum basics

Shift-left testing, Continuous Feedback, DevSecOps

Resources:

YouTube: “DevOps in 100 Seconds” by Fireship

Book: The Phoenix Project or Accelerate



⚙️ 2. Master Linux & Shell Scripting

Almost everything in DevOps runs on Linux.

Learn:

Basic Linux commands (cd, ls, grep, chmod, chown, etc.)

System monitoring (top, ps, df, du, free, netstat)

Bash scripting (loops, variables, conditionals, cron jobs)

File permissions, users, and environment variables

Practice:

Use WSL (Windows Subsystem for Linux) or a VM

Automate small tasks with shell scripts



🧱 3. Version Control – Git & GitHub/GitLab

You likely already know Git, but now focus on team-level and CI/CD use.

Learn:

Git branching strategies (Gitflow, trunk-based)

Pull requests & merge pipelines

Webhooks & Git tags for deployment triggers

Practice:

Automate builds when code is pushed to main branch



🧰 4. CI/CD Pipelines

Learn to automate your build, test, and deployment.

Tools:

GitHub Actions (beginner-friendly)

Jenkins (enterprise standard)

GitLab CI/CD, CircleCI, Bitbucket Pipelines

Learn:

Writing YAML pipeline files

Build → Test → Deploy automation

Deploying to staging/production environments

Secrets management in pipelines

Practice:

Deploy a Node.js or React app automatically to AWS EC2 or Vercel



🏗️ 5. Containerization – Docker

Docker is core to modern DevOps.

Learn:

Dockerfile basics (FROM, RUN, COPY, CMD)

docker build/run/ps/logs/exec

Docker volumes and networks

Docker Compose for multi-container setups

Practice:

Containerize your frontend + backend

Connect Node.js API and MongoDB using Docker Compose



☸️ 6. Container Orchestration – Kubernetes

Kubernetes manages containers at scale.

Learn:

Pods, Deployments, Services, ConfigMaps, Secrets

Ingress, Autoscaling, Namespaces

kubectl commands

Helm charts for templating

Practice:

Deploy a multi-service app (frontend + backend + DB) on Minikube or Kind




🧮 7. Infrastructure as Code (IaC)

Use code to create servers, networks, and storage.

Tools:

Terraform (industry standard)

AWS CloudFormation (AWS-specific)

Pulumi (for TypeScript users)

Learn:

Writing .tf files for EC2, S3, VPC, etc.

Variables, state, and modules

Remote backend & workspaces

Practice:

Deploy a full environment (server + DB + S3) with Terraform




☁️ 8. Cloud Platforms

You should pick one major cloud and go deep.

Choose one (and explore the basics):

AWS (most popular)

Google Cloud (GCP)

Azure

Learn:

Compute: EC2, Lambda, GCE

Storage: S3, Cloud Storage

Networking: VPC, Security Groups

CI/CD integrations (CodePipeline, Cloud Build)

Monitoring (CloudWatch, Stackdriver)

Certifications (optional):

AWS Certified Cloud Practitioner → DevOps Engineer




🔐 9. Monitoring, Logging & Alerting

Keep your apps healthy and observable.

Tools:

Prometheus + Grafana (metrics + dashboards)

ELK Stack (Elasticsearch, Logstash, Kibana)

Loki, Fluentd

CloudWatch / Datadog / New Relic

Learn:

Setting up alerts

Visualizing performance metrics

Log aggregation & tracing (OpenTelemetry)




🧠 10. Security & DevSecOps

Security must be integrated, not added later.

Learn:

Managing secrets (Vault, AWS Secrets Manager)

SSL/TLS certificates

SAST/DAST tools (SonarQube, OWASP ZAP)

Secure image scanning (Trivy, Anchore)




⚡ 11. Advanced Concepts

Once comfortable, explore:

Blue-Green & Canary deployments

GitOps (ArgoCD, Flux)

Serverless (AWS Lambda, GCP Functions)

Service Mesh (Istio)

Auto-scaling & Load balancing strategies



🧩 12. Project Practice

Put everything together.

Build Projects Like:

CI/CD pipeline for a Next.js + NestJS app (build → test → deploy → monitor)

Deploy full-stack app on AWS using Docker + Terraform + GitHub Actions

Kubernetes deployment with Prometheus + Grafana monitoring

Create an auto-scaling, load-balanced app using EC2 + RDS
